# Unreal project artefacts, for when the Amanda project is created beside the
# plugin. Everything here is regenerated by the engine or the compiler, and all
# of it is large.
Binaries/
Build/
DerivedDataCache/
Intermediate/
Saved/
*.sln
*.suo
*.VC.db
*.opendb

# The project's Plugins/AmandaBridge is a junction back to unreal/AmandaBridge
# in this same repo -- one copy of the plugin, editable from either path.
# Tracking it here would commit the plugin twice.
Amanda/Plugins/

# MetaHuman and Quixel assets are hundreds of megabytes of binary and come from
# Fab rather than from here. Content/ is deliberately not ignored wholesale --
# levels, Blueprints and the animation graph are the project -- so add specific
# asset directories here if they turn out to be too big to track.

# Third-party MetaHuman packages exported from Fab. Hundreds of megabytes
# each, redownloadable from the account that owns them, and not ours to
# redistribute.
Amanda/Import/

# The assembled character: ~500 MB of skeletal meshes, materials and textures,
# rebuilt from the Fab package by Scripts/import_metahuman.py and
# Scripts/assemble_metahuman.py. Derived data, not source. The look-dev level
# references it, so a fresh clone needs those scripts run before it opens.
Amanda/Content/MetaHumans/
Amanda/Content/Characters/
